      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DATA LEAK (3) has not been far away recently in town, and all of his 3 career wins have been on his home track here. He maps to receive a run to suit him, and jumping up 4kg in weight won't bother this tough gelding at this level. On top for us. ABRAHAM (2) was beaten as a loose $5 favourite at the Gold Coast 4 weeks ago, and after the race he was found to be mildly lame, explaining his poor performance. The front pads are off for the first time, which suggests he is over that issue, and he can make amends. Follow your money. SWITCHBLADE (5) had been running on over shorter trips before stepping up to 1500m, and storming home to score easily by 4 lengths. A repeat of that run, would make him hard to beat again. GOLDEN LOOM (4) is worth including.",
